From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:15:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] core: let the shell lay windows out on a transformed
 canvas

A shell can show windows on a canvas larger than the monitors by moving
them anywhere and transforming the window group to pan and zoom. Mutter
keeps windows on a monitor and its work area, snaps them to edges while
they are dragged, measures drags and Xwayland pointer positions in stage
coordinates, and culls hidden window areas against the stage without the
group's transform, so windows drift from the pointer and stop redrawing
once the group is scaled or moved.

A window's unconstrained property lets it be placed anywhere: the
onscreen, titlebar and single monitor constraints, edge resistance and
edge tiling leave it alone, and popups and dialogs follow their parent
without being slid or flipped back onto a monitor. Window drags,
Xwayland pointer coordinates and the unobscured regions are mapped
through the window group's transform, which leaves them unchanged while
the group is untransformed.
